# Environment for every sandbox shell and process, in both engines.
#
# This file is the declaration. A Containerfile ENV cannot serve the guest: sshd
# resets the environment for every session, so `ssh <name>` and `ssh <name> cmd`
# see none of it, and a microVM never had it at all — its rootfs is a
# `podman export`, which carries files but not image config.
#
# So anything a guest needs at RUNTIME belongs here, and nowhere else. Adding a
# line is the whole change: .bashrc replays this for shells and the microVM's
# PID 1 replays it for the process tree. Re-declaring variables by hand instead
# is what let CHROME_BIN and the DISABLE_* pair drift out of sync.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, one per line, values literal (no expansion). Anything
# already set wins, so --env injection and a user's own export are never
# overridden. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.

# Headless browser, for tools that resolve one via CHROME_BIN (e.g. Playwright's
# executablePath). The image ships Chromium.
CHROME_BIN=/usr/bin/chromium-browser

# Claude Code is a pinned binary in read-only /opt, which matches none of its
# known installMethods — so its install-health check nags, and its auto-updater
# would shadow-install a newer build into ~/.local. Both off.
DISABLE_INSTALLATION_CHECKS=1
DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1
